IMPORT prelude
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g1-interpretation`
IMPORT `g1-art1-defined-terms`
IMPORT `g1-art2-entity`

-- g1-tests-art2-entity.l4: tests of Article 2(1) to (6), with every expected value decided from the source before the module was run.
-- The bodies are described by the list of things true of them (a witness's statements), and a builder turns that list into the record the rules take.

§ `Part 1 — Interpretation: tests of Article 2(1) to (6)`

§§ `The bodies`

-- Test-only: one constructor per question the record asks; a body is described by the statements that are true of it, and everything else is false.
DECLARE `A thing true of a body` IS ONE OF
    `it is the trustees of a trust`
    `it is the fidéicommissaires of a court-approved fidéicommis`
    `it is a body corporate`
    `it is an NPO`
    `it is established under the law of Jersey`
    `it is an incorporated 1862 association`
    `it is a foundation`
    `it was established by an enactment`
    `it was established by Act of the States`
    `it was established by Royal Charter`
    `it was established in relation to Jersey`
    `it is a company`
    `it is incorporated under, but not by, an enactment`
    `it is incorporated under, but not by, a UK Act`
    `it is an unincorporated body`
    `it is a partnership`
    `it is established under the law of another jurisdiction`
    `its relationship is governed by the law of Jersey`

GIVEN true IS A LIST OF `A thing true of a body`
      similar IS A LIST OF `Kind of entity`
      added IS A LIST OF STRING
      lawName IS A MAYBE STRING
      enactment IS A MAYBE STRING
      people IS A LIST OF Governor
GIVETH A `Facts about the body under Article 2`
`a body with details` true similar added lawName enactment people MEANS
    `Facts about the body under Article 2` WITH
        `the person or persons, taken together, who are the trustees of a trust` IS elem `it is the trustees of a trust` true
        `the person or persons, taken together, who are the fidéicommissaires of a court-approved fidéicommis` IS elem `it is the fidéicommissaires of a court-approved fidéicommis` true
        `a body corporate` IS elem `it is a body corporate` true
        `an NPO, as defined by the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008` IS elem `it is an NPO` true
        `established under the law of Jersey` IS elem `it is established under the law of Jersey` true
        `an association incorporated under Article 4 of the Loi of 1862` IS elem `it is an incorporated 1862 association` true
        `a foundation under the Foundations (Jersey) Law 2009` IS elem `it is a foundation` true
        `established by an enactment` IS elem `it was established by an enactment` true
        `established by Act of the States` IS elem `it was established by Act of the States` true
        `established by Royal Charter` IS elem `it was established by Royal Charter` true
        `established in relation to Jersey` IS elem `it was established in relation to Jersey` true
        `the Law by which the body corporate was established` IS lawName
        `a company under the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991` IS elem `it is a company` true
        `incorporated under, but not by, an enactment other than the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991` IS elem `it is incorporated under, but not by, an enactment` true
        `incorporated under, but not by, an Act of the United Kingdom Parliament or Order in Council, as such Act or Order is extended to or applicable in Jersey` IS elem `it is incorporated under, but not by, a UK Act` true
        `the enactment under which the body was incorporated` IS enactment
        `the persons, taken together, who constitute for the time being an unincorporated body or association of persons` IS elem `it is an unincorporated body` true
        `a partnership` IS elem `it is a partnership` true
        `the kinds mentioned in sub-paragraphs (a) to (h) that the body is substantially similar to` IS similar
        `established under the law of a jurisdiction other than Jersey` IS elem `it is established under the law of another jurisdiction` true
        `the law governing the relationship between the persons constituting it, in that capacity, is the law of Jersey` IS elem `its relationship is governed by the law of Jersey` true
        `the sub-paragraphs added by Order within which the body falls` IS added
        governors IS people

GIVEN true IS A LIST OF `A thing true of a body`
GIVETH A `Facts about the body under Article 2`
`a body of which only these are true` true MEANS
    `a body with details` true EMPTY EMPTY NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY

-- A governor of the kinds Article 2(3)(b)(ii) tells apart.
GIVEN natural IS A BOOLEAN
      resident IS A BOOLEAN
      byA IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Governor
`a governor who is` natural `natural,` resident `resident in Jersey and` byA `a Jersey entity by (a)` MEANS
    Governor WITH
        name IS "Test Governor"
        `is a natural person` IS natural
        `is resident in Jersey` IS resident
        `is itself a Jersey entity by virtue of Article 2(3)(a)` IS byA
        `reportable matters` IS EMPTY

-- The same body in the text of 2 October 2026, in the favoured reading.
GIVEN body IS A `Facts about the body under Article 2`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Kind of entity`
`the kinds of` body MEANS
    `Art 2(1) the kinds of entity the body falls within` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `the text of 2 October 2026` body

-- The bodies, one per sub-paragraph.
`a trust` MEANS `a body of which only these are true` (LIST `it is the trustees of a trust`)
`a fidéicommis` MEANS `a body of which only these are true` (LIST `it is the fidéicommissaires of a court-approved fidéicommis`)
`an NPO body corporate` MEANS `a body of which only these are true` (LIST `it is a body corporate`, `it is an NPO`, `it is established under the law of Jersey`)
`an 1862 association` MEANS `a body of which only these are true` (LIST `it is an incorporated 1862 association`)
`a foundation body` MEANS `a body of which only these are true` (LIST `it is a foundation`)
`a company body` MEANS `a body of which only these are true` (LIST `it is a body corporate`, `it is a company`)
`a body incorporated under an enactment` MEANS `a body of which only these are true` (LIST `it is a body corporate`, `it is incorporated under, but not by, an enactment`)
`a body incorporated under a UK Act` MEANS `a body of which only these are true` (LIST `it is a body corporate`, `it is incorporated under, but not by, a UK Act`)
`an unincorporated association` MEANS `a body of which only these are true` (LIST `it is an unincorporated body`)

§§ `2(1) the kinds of entity`

-- (a) to (h) and (i), each on its own, in the text of 2 October 2026.
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `a trust` EQUALS LIST `the trustees of a trust`
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `a fidéicommis` EQUALS LIST `the fidéicommissaires of a court-approved fidéicommis`
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `an NPO body corporate` EQUALS LIST `a body corporate that is an NPO established under the law of Jersey`
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `an 1862 association` EQUALS LIST `an incorporated 1862 association`
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `a foundation body` EQUALS LIST `a foundation`
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `a company body` EQUALS LIST `a company`
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `a body incorporated under an enactment` EQUALS LIST `a body incorporated under, but not by, an enactment other than the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991`
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `a body incorporated under a UK Act` EQUALS LIST `a body incorporated under, but not by, an Act of the United Kingdom Parliament or Order in Council`
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `an unincorporated association` EQUALS LIST `an unincorporated body or association of persons`

-- A body with none of the statements true is not an entity.
`a body that is nothing` MEANS `a body of which only these are true` EMPTY
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `a body that is nothing` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(1) the body is an entity` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `the text of 2 October 2026` `a body that is nothing`
#ASSERT `Art 2(1) the body is an entity` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `the text of 2 October 2026` `a trust`

-- (e): a body corporate established (i) by an enactment, (ii) by Act of the States, or (iii) by Royal Charter, in relation to Jersey.
`a body established by an enactment in relation to Jersey` MEANS
    `a body of which only these are true` (LIST `it is a body corporate`, `it was established by an enactment`, `it was established in relation to Jersey`)
`a body established by Act of the States` MEANS
    `a body of which only these are true` (LIST `it is a body corporate`, `it was established by Act of the States`)
`a body established by Royal Charter in relation to Jersey` MEANS
    `a body of which only these are true` (LIST `it is a body corporate`, `it was established by Royal Charter`, `it was established in relation to Jersey`)
`a body established by Royal Charter not in relation to Jersey` MEANS
    `a body of which only these are true` (LIST `it is a body corporate`, `it was established by Royal Charter`)
`a body established by an enactment not in relation to Jersey` MEANS
    `a body of which only these are true` (LIST `it is a body corporate`, `it was established by an enactment`)
`an unincorporated body established by an enactment` MEANS
    `a body of which only these are true` (LIST `it was established by an enactment`, `it was established in relation to Jersey`)

#ASSERT `the kinds of` `a body established by an enactment in relation to Jersey` EQUALS LIST `a body corporate established by an enactment, an Act of the States or a Royal Charter`
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `a body established by Royal Charter in relation to Jersey` EQUALS LIST `a body corporate established by an enactment, an Act of the States or a Royal Charter`

-- The discriminating case of F1.6: "in relation to Jersey" after Royal Charter. A charter not in relation to Jersey is out on both readings; an enactment or an Act of the States
-- with no stated relation to Jersey is in on reading A (taken) and out on reading B.
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `a body established by Royal Charter not in relation to Jersey` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `Art 2(1) the kinds of entity the body falls within` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.6 read the other way` `the text of 2 October 2026` `a body established by Royal Charter not in relation to Jersey` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `a body established by an enactment not in relation to Jersey` EQUALS LIST `a body corporate established by an enactment, an Act of the States or a Royal Charter`
#ASSERT `Art 2(1) the kinds of entity the body falls within` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.6 read the other way` `the text of 2 October 2026` `a body established by an enactment not in relation to Jersey` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `a body established by Act of the States` EQUALS LIST `a body corporate established by an enactment, an Act of the States or a Royal Charter`
#ASSERT `Art 2(1) the kinds of entity the body falls within` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.6 read the other way` `the text of 2 October 2026` `a body established by Act of the States` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `Art 2(1) the kinds of entity the body falls within` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.6 read the other way` `the text of 2 October 2026` `a body established by an enactment in relation to Jersey` EQUALS LIST `a body corporate established by an enactment, an Act of the States or a Royal Charter`
#ASSERT `Art 2(1) the kinds of entity the body falls within` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.6 read the other way` `the text of 2 October 2026` `a body established by Royal Charter in relation to Jersey` EQUALS LIST `a body corporate established by an enactment, an Act of the States or a Royal Charter`

-- (e) is a body corporate: the same statements without "it is a body corporate" give nothing.
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `an unincorporated body established by an enactment` EQUALS EMPTY

-- Each reading is a callable function of its own.
#ASSERT `Art 2(1)(e) reading A: in relation to Jersey qualifies the Royal Charter only` `a body established by an enactment not in relation to Jersey`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(1)(e) reading B: in relation to Jersey qualifies each of (i), (ii) and (iii)` `a body established by an enactment not in relation to Jersey`
#ASSERT `Art 2(1)(e)(i) the body corporate is established by an enactment` `a body established by an enactment not in relation to Jersey`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(1)(e)(ii) the body corporate is established by Act of the States` `a body established by an enactment not in relation to Jersey`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(1)(e)(iii) the body corporate is established by Royal Charter` `a body established by an enactment not in relation to Jersey`

-- A body in more than one kind: a company that is the sole trustee of a trust is (a) and (f) (Article 8(3)(a)(i): "whether it also falls within sub-paragraph (a)"), listed in the Law's order.
`a company that is the sole trustee` MEANS
    `a body of which only these are true` (LIST `it is the trustees of a trust`, `it is a body corporate`, `it is a company`)
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `a company that is the sole trustee` EQUALS LIST `the trustees of a trust`, `a company`

-- (b) is "without prejudice to the generality of sub-paragraph (a)": a court-approved fidéicommis that is also a trust is in (a) and (b), in the Law's order.
`a fidéicommis that is also a trust` MEANS
    `a body of which only these are true` (LIST `it is the trustees of a trust`, `it is the fidéicommissaires of a court-approved fidéicommis`)
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `a fidéicommis that is also a trust` EQUALS LIST `the trustees of a trust`, `the fidéicommissaires of a court-approved fidéicommis`

-- (g) and (h) with a company: all three.
`a company that is also within (g) and (h)` MEANS
    `a body of which only these are true` (LIST `it is the trustees of a trust`, `it is a body corporate`, `it is a company`, `it is incorporated under, but not by, an enactment`, `it is incorporated under, but not by, a UK Act`)
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `a company that is also within (g) and (h)` EQUALS LIST `the trustees of a trust`, `a company`, `a body incorporated under, but not by, an enactment other than the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991`, `a body incorporated under, but not by, an Act of the United Kingdom Parliament or Order in Council`

§§ `2(1)(g): does it overlap (c), (d) and (f)? (fork F1.8)`

`a foundation also incorporated under an enactment` MEANS
    `a body of which only these are true` (LIST `it is a body corporate`, `it is a foundation`, `it is incorporated under, but not by, an enactment`)
`an 1862 association also incorporated under an enactment` MEANS
    `a body of which only these are true` (LIST `it is a body corporate`, `it is an incorporated 1862 association`, `it is incorporated under, but not by, an enactment`)

-- As written (taken): a foundation, incorporated under the Foundations (Jersey) Law 2009, an enactment other than the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991, is in (d) and in (g).
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `a foundation also incorporated under an enactment` EQUALS LIST `a foundation`, `a body incorporated under, but not by, an enactment other than the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991`
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `an 1862 association also incorporated under an enactment` EQUALS LIST `an incorporated 1862 association`, `a body incorporated under, but not by, an enactment other than the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991`
-- The residue reading: (g) leaves out a body that is already within (c), (d) or (f).
#ASSERT `Art 2(1) the kinds of entity the body falls within` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.8 read the other way` `the text of 2 October 2026` `a foundation also incorporated under an enactment` EQUALS LIST `a foundation`
#ASSERT `Art 2(1) the kinds of entity the body falls within` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.8 read the other way` `the text of 2 October 2026` `an 1862 association also incorporated under an enactment` EQUALS LIST `an incorporated 1862 association`
-- A body within (g) alone is in (g) on both readings; a company's (g) flag is dropped on the residue reading.
#ASSERT `Art 2(1) the kinds of entity the body falls within` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.8 read the other way` `the text of 2 October 2026` `a body incorporated under an enactment` EQUALS LIST `a body incorporated under, but not by, an enactment other than the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991`
#ASSERT `Art 2(1) the kinds of entity the body falls within` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.8 read the other way` `the text of 2 October 2026` `a company that is also within (g) and (h)` EQUALS LIST `the trustees of a trust`, `a company`, `a body incorporated under, but not by, an Act of the United Kingdom Parliament or Order in Council`
-- Each reading is a callable function of its own.
#ASSERT `Art 2(1)(g) the body is incorporated under, but not by, an enactment other than the Companies Law` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `a foundation also incorporated under an enactment`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(1)(g) the body is incorporated under, but not by, an enactment other than the Companies Law` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.8 read the other way` `a foundation also incorporated under an enactment`

§§ `2(1)(i): an unincorporated body, other than a partnership and other than the trustees of a trust`

`an unincorporated partnership` MEANS `a body of which only these are true` (LIST `it is an unincorporated body`, `it is a partnership`)
`an unincorporated body that is the trustees of a trust` MEANS `a body of which only these are true` (LIST `it is an unincorporated body`, `it is the trustees of a trust`)
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `an unincorporated partnership` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `an unincorporated body that is the trustees of a trust` EQUALS LIST `the trustees of a trust`

§§ `2(1)(ba): the text of 16 October 2025`

-- R&O.56/2025 was made on 9 October 2025 and came into force 7 days after, on 16 October 2025: (ba) is in the text of 16 October 2025 and the text of 2 October 2026, and in no earlier text.
-- The text of 15 October 2025 is the text of 27 February 2024 (the Table of Legislation History has no text between them).
#ASSERT `Art 2(1) the kinds of entity the body falls within` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `the text of 16 October 2025` `an NPO body corporate` EQUALS LIST `a body corporate that is an NPO established under the law of Jersey`
#ASSERT `Art 2(1) the kinds of entity the body falls within` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `the text of 2 October 2026` `an NPO body corporate` EQUALS LIST `a body corporate that is an NPO established under the law of Jersey`
#ASSERT `Art 2(1) the kinds of entity the body falls within` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `the text of 27 February 2024` `an NPO body corporate` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `Art 2(1) the kinds of entity the body falls within` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `the text of 12 April 2023` `an NPO body corporate` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `Art 2(1) the kinds of entity the body falls within` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `the text of 2 March 2021` `an NPO body corporate` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `Art 2(1) the kinds of entity the body falls within` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `the text of 1 January 2020` `an NPO body corporate` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `Art 2(1) the kinds of entity the body falls within` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `the text of 16 December 2019` `an NPO body corporate` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `Art 2(1) the kinds of entity the body falls within` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `the text of 31 May 2019` `an NPO body corporate` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `Art 2(1) the kinds of entity the body falls within` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `the text of 1 January 2019` `an NPO body corporate` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 2(1) the kinds of entity the body falls within` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `before the first consolidated version` `an NPO body corporate`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 2(1) the kinds of entity the body falls within` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `before the first consolidated version` `a trust`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(1) the body is an entity` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `the text of 27 February 2024` `an NPO body corporate`
#ASSERT `Art 2(1) the body is an entity` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `the text of 16 October 2025` `an NPO body corporate`
#ASSERT `Art 2(1)(ba) is part of the text of` `the text of 16 October 2025`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(1)(ba) is part of the text of` `the text of 27 February 2024`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 2(1)(ba) is part of the text of` `before the first consolidated version`

-- The other sub-paragraphs are the same in every text from 1 January 2019: a trust is an entity in each.
#ASSERT `Art 2(1) the kinds of entity the body falls within` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `the text of 1 January 2019` `a trust` EQUALS LIST `the trustees of a trust`
#ASSERT `Art 2(1) the kinds of entity the body falls within` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `the text of 27 February 2024` `a trust` EQUALS LIST `the trustees of a trust`

-- (ba)(i), (ii) and (iii): each limb on its own.
`a body corporate that is not an NPO` MEANS `a body of which only these are true` (LIST `it is a body corporate`, `it is established under the law of Jersey`)
`an NPO body corporate not established under Jersey law` MEANS `a body of which only these are true` (LIST `it is a body corporate`, `it is an NPO`)
`an NPO and Jersey-established body that is not corporate` MEANS `a body of which only these are true` (LIST `it is an NPO`, `it is established under the law of Jersey`)
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `a body corporate that is not an NPO` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `an NPO body corporate not established under Jersey law` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `an NPO and Jersey-established body that is not corporate` EQUALS EMPTY

-- (iii): an NPO body corporate established under Jersey law that falls within any of (c) to (h) is in that sub-paragraph and not in (ba).
`an NPO that is an 1862 association` MEANS `a body of which only these are true` (LIST `it is a body corporate`, `it is an NPO`, `it is established under the law of Jersey`, `it is an incorporated 1862 association`)
`an NPO that is a foundation` MEANS `a body of which only these are true` (LIST `it is a body corporate`, `it is an NPO`, `it is established under the law of Jersey`, `it is a foundation`)
`an NPO that is established by an enactment` MEANS `a body of which only these are true` (LIST `it is a body corporate`, `it is an NPO`, `it is established under the law of Jersey`, `it was established by an enactment`, `it was established in relation to Jersey`)
`an NPO that is a company` MEANS `a body of which only these are true` (LIST `it is a body corporate`, `it is an NPO`, `it is established under the law of Jersey`, `it is a company`)
`an NPO incorporated under an enactment` MEANS `a body of which only these are true` (LIST `it is a body corporate`, `it is an NPO`, `it is established under the law of Jersey`, `it is incorporated under, but not by, an enactment`)
`an NPO incorporated under a UK Act` MEANS `a body of which only these are true` (LIST `it is a body corporate`, `it is an NPO`, `it is established under the law of Jersey`, `it is incorporated under, but not by, a UK Act`)
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `an NPO that is an 1862 association` EQUALS LIST `an incorporated 1862 association`
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `an NPO that is a foundation` EQUALS LIST `a foundation`
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `an NPO that is established by an enactment` EQUALS LIST `a body corporate established by an enactment, an Act of the States or a Royal Charter`
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `an NPO that is a company` EQUALS LIST `a company`
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `an NPO incorporated under an enactment` EQUALS LIST `a body incorporated under, but not by, an enactment other than the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991`
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `an NPO incorporated under a UK Act` EQUALS LIST `a body incorporated under, but not by, an Act of the United Kingdom Parliament or Order in Council`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(1)(ba)(iii) the body falls within one of sub-paragraphs (c) to (h)` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `an NPO body corporate`
#ASSERT `Art 2(1)(ba)(iii) the body falls within one of sub-paragraphs (c) to (h)` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `an NPO that is a company`

-- (ba) is not excluded by (a): an NPO body corporate that is also the trustees of a trust is in (a) and (ba); sub-paragraph (iii) lists (c) to (h) only.
`an NPO body corporate that is the sole trustee` MEANS
    `a body of which only these are true` (LIST `it is the trustees of a trust`, `it is a body corporate`, `it is an NPO`, `it is established under the law of Jersey`)
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `an NPO body corporate that is the sole trustee` EQUALS LIST `the trustees of a trust`, `a body corporate that is an NPO established under the law of Jersey`

§§ `2(1)(j): an entity substantially similar to one in (a) to (h), established under the law of another jurisdiction (fork F1.1)`

-- The kinds the body is substantially similar to are a judgement and an input.
GIVEN similar IS A LIST OF `Kind of entity`
      foreign IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts about the body under Article 2`
`a foreign body similar to` similar `, established elsewhere:` foreign MEANS
    `a body with details`
        (IF foreign THEN LIST `it is established under the law of another jurisdiction` ELSE EMPTY)
        similar EMPTY NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY

`a foreign company` MEANS `a foreign body similar to` (LIST `a company`) `, established elsewhere:` TRUE
`a foreign body similar to an NPO body corporate` MEANS `a foreign body similar to` (LIST `a body corporate that is an NPO established under the law of Jersey`) `, established elsewhere:` TRUE
`a Jersey body said to be similar to a company` MEANS `a foreign body similar to` (LIST `a company`) `, established elsewhere:` FALSE
`a foreign body similar to nothing` MEANS `a foreign body similar to` EMPTY `, established elsewhere:` TRUE
`a foreign body similar to an unincorporated body` MEANS `a foreign body similar to` (LIST `an unincorporated body or association of persons`) `, established elsewhere:` TRUE
`a foreign body similar to a foreign body` MEANS `a foreign body similar to` (LIST `an entity substantially similar to one of the above, established under the law of another jurisdiction`) `, established elsewhere:` TRUE

#ASSERT `the kinds of` `a foreign company` EQUALS LIST `an entity substantially similar to one of the above, established under the law of another jurisdiction`
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `a Jersey body said to be similar to a company` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `a foreign body similar to nothing` EQUALS EMPTY

-- (j) names "sub-paragraphs (a) to (h)": similarity to (i) or to (j) itself does not count.
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `a foreign body similar to an unincorporated body` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the kinds of` `a foreign body similar to a foreign body` EQUALS EMPTY

-- F1.1: is the inserted (ba) inside "(a) to (h)"? Reading A (taken): yes by the letters, so a foreign analogue of an NPO body corporate is within (j) in the texts that have (ba).
#ASSERT `Art 2(1) the kinds of entity the body falls within` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `the text of 2 October 2026` `a foreign body similar to an NPO body corporate` EQUALS LIST `an entity substantially similar to one of the above, established under the law of another jurisdiction`
#ASSERT `Art 2(1) the kinds of entity the body falls within` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `the text of 16 October 2025` `a foreign body similar to an NPO body corporate` EQUALS LIST `an entity substantially similar to one of the above, established under the law of another jurisdiction`
#ASSERT `Art 2(1) the kinds of entity the body falls within` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.1 read the other way` `the text of 2 October 2026` `a foreign body similar to an NPO body corporate` EQUALS EMPTY
-- In the text of 27 February 2024 there is no (ba) to be similar to, on either reading.
#ASSERT `Art 2(1) the kinds of entity the body falls within` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `the text of 27 February 2024` `a foreign body similar to an NPO body corporate` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `Art 2(1) the kinds of entity the body falls within` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.1 read the other way` `the text of 27 February 2024` `a foreign body similar to an NPO body corporate` EQUALS EMPTY
-- The range itself.
