§§ `2(6) purpose`

#ASSERT `Art 2(6) the purpose of the entity means` `the trustees of a trust` EQUALS "the benefit of its beneficiaries or any other purpose mentioned in Article 2(b) of the Trusts (Jersey) Law 1984 by virtue of which the trust exists, as specified in its constitution"
#ASSERT `Art 2(6) the purpose of the entity means` `the fidéicommissaires of a court-approved fidéicommis` EQUALS "the objects for which it was created or incorporated, or that were subsequently authorized under Article 10 of the Loi of 1862"
#ASSERT `Art 2(6) the purpose of the entity means` `an incorporated 1862 association` EQUALS "the objects for which it was created or incorporated, or that were subsequently authorized under Article 10 of the Loi of 1862"
#ASSERT `Art 2(6) the purpose of the entity means` `a foundation` EQUALS "the objects specified in its charter or its regulations"
-- (d) any other entity: a company, an unincorporated body, a body added by an Order, and every other kind.
#ASSERT `Art 2(6) the purpose of the entity means` `a company` EQUALS "a purpose to which that entity’s property may lawfully be applied, other than by virtue of an order of a court, in accordance with the powers of the entity as set out in its constitution (including on its winding up or other termination)"
#ASSERT `Art 2(6) the purpose of the entity means` `an unincorporated body or association of persons` EQUALS "a purpose to which that entity’s property may lawfully be applied, other than by virtue of an order of a court, in accordance with the powers of the entity as set out in its constitution (including on its winding up or other termination)"
#ASSERT `Art 2(6) the purpose of the entity means` `a body corporate that is an NPO established under the law of Jersey` EQUALS "a purpose to which that entity’s property may lawfully be applied, other than by virtue of an order of a court, in accordance with the powers of the entity as set out in its constitution (including on its winding up or other termination)"
#ASSERT `Art 2(6) the purpose of the entity means` (`an entity added by an Order under Article 2(2)` "(k)") EQUALS "a purpose to which that entity’s property may lawfully be applied, other than by virtue of an order of a court, in accordance with the powers of the entity as set out in its constitution (including on its winding up or other termination)"
-- F1.4: a company that is the sole trustee has the trust's purposes and its own (reading A), or the trust's only (reading B).
#ASSERT `Art 2(6) the purposes of the entity in all its kinds mean` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` (LIST `the trustees of a trust`, `a company`) EQUALS LIST "the benefit of its beneficiaries or any other purpose mentioned in Article 2(b) of the Trusts (Jersey) Law 1984 by virtue of which the trust exists, as specified in its constitution"
#ASSERT `Art 2(6) the purposes of the entity in all its kinds mean` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.4 read the other way` (LIST `the trustees of a trust`, `a company`) EQUALS LIST "the benefit of its beneficiaries or any other purpose mentioned in Article 2(b) of the Trusts (Jersey) Law 1984 by virtue of which the trust exists, as specified in its constitution"
-- (d) is "any other entity": it does not add to a trust's purposes when (a) applies, and a company that is also (a) is not "any other entity".
#ASSERT `Art 2(6) the purposes of the entity in all its kinds mean` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` (LIST `a company`) EQUALS LIST "a purpose to which that entity’s property may lawfully be applied, other than by virtue of an order of a court, in accordance with the powers of the entity as set out in its constitution (including on its winding up or other termination)"
#ASSERT `Art 2(6) the purposes of the entity in all its kinds mean` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` (LIST `the trustees of a trust`, `a foundation`) EQUALS LIST "the benefit of its beneficiaries or any other purpose mentioned in Article 2(b) of the Trusts (Jersey) Law 1984 by virtue of which the trust exists, as specified in its constitution", "the objects specified in its charter or its regulations"
#ASSERT `Art 2(6) the purposes of the entity in all its kinds mean` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.4 read the other way` (LIST `a foundation`, `the trustees of a trust`) EQUALS LIST "the benefit of its beneficiaries or any other purpose mentioned in Article 2(b) of the Trusts (Jersey) Law 1984 by virtue of which the trust exists, as specified in its constitution"
#ASSERT `Art 2(6) the purposes of the entity in all its kinds mean` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` EMPTY EQUALS EMPTY
